<Base lang="en-US" pageType="Article" adKind="article" title="Gaucho Pants Origin: The History of Bombachas and Traditional Dress" description="Where did gaucho pants come from? Learn about Argentine bombachas, traditional riding trousers, the contested Ottoman connection, and older chiripá clothing.">
<article class="en-article"><nav class="crumb"><a href="/en/">English edition</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a></nav><header><p class="eyebrow">ENGLISH RESEARCH · GAUCHO HISTORY & LITERATURE</p><h1>Gaucho Pants Origin: The History of Bombachas and Traditional Dress</h1><p class="lead">The loose trousers associated with Argentine gauchos are often called bombachas de campo. Their history is more complicated than the idea of a single timeless gaucho uniform—and claims about their origin need dated evidence.</p></header><figure><img src="/media/cultura-gauchesca/poncho-chiripa-vestimenta-gaucha.webp" alt="Modern editorial reconstruction illustrating the cultural world of Martín Fierro" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Modern editorial illustration, not an authentic historical photograph.</figcaption></figure><div class="body"><nav class="toc"><strong>Contents</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a>)}<a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>{sections.map((s,i)=><><section id={s.id}><h2>{s.heading}</h2><p>{s.body}</p></section>{i===0&&<AdSlot id="article-02-post-introduction" kind="article"/>}{i===2&&<AdSlot id="article-03-middle" kind="article"/>}{i===4&&<AdSlot id="article-04-late" kind="article"/>}</>)}<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><p>This article distinguishes documented historical claims, scholarly interpretation and literary representation. Historical material is linked to the source institution or publication; original Spanish verses have not been modified or republished in translation here.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('https://')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('https://')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul><p><a href="/en/martin-fierro-summary/">Plot summary</a> · <a href="/en/what-is-a-gaucho/">Gaucho history</a> · <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a></p></section><AdSlot id="article-05-end" kind="article"/></div></article>
